+      "type": "text",
+      "title": "Where they go, and the commas",
+      "content": "A stance adverb can open the sentence, sit in the middle or close it, and a comma marks each edge: *En realidad, la calle era más mezclada.* / *La calle, en realidad, era más mezclada.* Right after the verb with no commas, the same word usually describes how something was done: *Sor Juana defendió rotundamente el derecho de las mujeres a estudiar*. *Apenas* and *precisamente* take no commas, because they point at the word right after them."
