+      "title": "What you already know",
+      "content": "You know *un servicio del que dependen muchas personas* and *el edificio en el que vivimos* from B1 Unit 20: when a relative clause needs a preposition, the preposition goes before *el que, la que, los que* or *las que*, matching the noun. On the border this pattern is everywhere: the checkpoint *por la que* people cross, the song *en la que* stories are told, the city *en la que* two cultures mix."
     },
     {
       "type": "table",
-      "title": "Estructuras relativas preposicionales",
